<Placemark><name>ccg/2026/NW-M-1525</name><styleUrl>#a</styleUrl><description>2026-10-21T18:18:00Z to until cancelled

Scientific Instruments Change - Browns Bank
Wave Glider C34164NS is remotely offloading data from bottom-mounted VR4-UWM acoustic receivers within an area bound by:

 42 28.786N 066 19.959W
42 13.393N 065 49.906W,
42 19.094N 065 43.026W,
42 24.323N 065 43.190W.
Wave glider c34164ns is copper in colour with a mast extending 1.2 metres above the surface of the water, supporting a solid white light and orange visibility flag and is equipped with a non-transmitting ais receiver. It is remotely operated, moving at a speed of approximately 1.2 knots and measuring 3.05 metres by 0.81 metres.
For further information, authorities and mariners may contact sue l’orsa at 250-877-8052, tyler byrne at 902-719-7078, or liquid robotics wave glider operations centre at +1 888-574-4574 or 408-636-4205.
                                                    Cancels NW-M-1487-26</description><MultiGeometry><Point><coordinates>-66.3327,42.4798,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-65.8318,42.2232,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-65.7171,42.3182,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-65.7198,42.4054,0</coordinates></Point></MultiGeometry></Placemark>
