<Placemark><name>ccg/2025/NW-C-3763</name><styleUrl>#a</styleUrl><description>2025-12-10T16:02:00Z to until cancelled

Waterway Information - Port of Trois-Rivieres, Trois-Rivières to Donnacona - Trois-Rivières
The Canadian Coast Guard published the VN-200 chart aimed at identifying maintained depths of the Saint Lawrence Waterway including certain anchorage areas.
Considering the natural over-depth observed at the TR1 anchorage station in the port of Trois-Rivières, it has been agreed to exceptionally allow a depth of 11.3 meters instead of 10.7 meters.
This depth is observed within the polygon defined by the following coordinates:
Point A : 46 20.227N 072 32.454W
Point B : 46 20.157N 072 32.060W
Point C : 46 20.074N 072 32.040W
Point D : 46 19.557N 072 32.892W
Point E : 46 19.560N 072 32.897W
Point F : 46 19.639N 072 32.921W
Point G : 46 19.950N 072 32.661W
Point H : 46 20.093N 072 32.550W
In order to obtain an anchoring authorization, every vessel is required to communicate and comply with the procedures established by the Trois-Rivières Port Authority.
 
                                                    Cancels NW-C-3760-25</description><MultiGeometry><Point><coordinates>-72.5409,46.3371,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-72.5343,46.3359,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-72.534,46.3346,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-72.5482,46.3259,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-72.5483,46.326,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-72.5487,46.3273,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-72.5443,46.3325,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-72.5425,46.3349,0</coordinates></Point></MultiGeometry></Placemark>
